WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.467
-Thank you so much
for coming on

00:00:02.467 --> 00:00:03.834
and especially around this --
this time of year.

00:00:03.834 --> 00:00:05.434
-Hi, everyone.
-Yeah, I want to get into

00:00:05.434 --> 00:00:07.467
all the Halloween stuff that
you -- I know you love doing.

00:00:07.467 --> 00:00:09.567
-My Halloween shenanigans.
-Yes, but I want to --

00:00:09.567 --> 00:00:10.934
There's so many things
I want to talk to you about.

00:00:10.934 --> 00:00:13.300
"America's Got Talent:
Fantasy League."

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:14.734
-Yes.
-What is it?

00:00:14.734 --> 00:00:16.033
How do we
explain it to everybody?

00:00:16.033 --> 00:00:18.400
-So, "Fantasy League,"
this is like a new spin-off show

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:20.000
that we do of
"America's Got Talent."

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.968
So this time around,
Mel B is back,

00:00:21.968 --> 00:00:23.667
which I'm excited
to see Mel again.

00:00:23.667 --> 00:00:25.033
-Good.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:25.033 --> 00:00:27.868
-And obviously Simon Cowell,
Howie Mandel, Terry Crews.

00:00:27.868 --> 00:00:31.434
But for this time around, we get
to, like, have our own team.

00:00:31.434 --> 00:00:34.434
So how we got about this
was very funny

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:37.067
because you had to have
a long straw,

00:00:37.067 --> 00:00:39.701
medium straw or shorter straw,
shortest straw,

00:00:39.701 --> 00:00:42.501
and whoever pulls the longest
straw gets to choose first.

00:00:42.501 --> 00:00:44.100
Guess who picked
the longest straw.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:46.400
-Yeah!
-I did. So that was amazing.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:49.100
So I bolted for everyone
who I loved.

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:50.968
Guess who had
the shortest stick.

00:00:50.968 --> 00:00:52.701
-Simon?
-It was Simon.

00:00:52.701 --> 00:00:54.200
[ Laughter ]
I was so excited.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:57.634
So he was always last
to draw your favorite act.

00:00:57.634 --> 00:01:01.267
So everyone has 10 acts,
and then we get to mentor them

00:01:01.267 --> 00:01:03.667
and help them, hopefully
make their act even better.

00:01:03.667 --> 00:01:07.067
-It's like a little
extra stuff in the line. Yeah.

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:08.601
-So I was like, "Okay.
What are we getting?"

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:11.634
Because, you know,
they get $250,000.

00:01:11.634 --> 00:01:13.033
And they were like,
"Well, nothing."

00:01:13.033 --> 00:01:15.467
And I'm like, "No, we need
to have something."

00:01:15.467 --> 00:01:17.334
Like, at least we have to have,
like, a little...

00:01:17.334 --> 00:01:18.934
-A trophy or something.
-I'm sure a trophy or something,

00:01:18.934 --> 00:01:20.567
but I'm sure that Simon
is making, like,

00:01:20.567 --> 00:01:23.200
a bobblehead doll of himself
or something like that.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:24.868
-How is your --
How is your team?

00:01:24.868 --> 00:01:26.868
-My team is the best team!
I mean, I can't tell you

00:01:26.868 --> 00:01:28.601
who's on the team.
You have to watch and see it.

00:01:28.601 --> 00:01:31.801
But, you know, America got
to vote on who they want,

00:01:31.801 --> 00:01:34.100
you know, those acts to be.
-So it's the best.

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:36.033
-So we had all of these acts
to choose from.

00:01:36.033 --> 00:01:37.934
But I had the longest stick,
so I got --

00:01:37.934 --> 00:01:39.367
I feel like
I have the best one.

00:01:39.367 --> 00:01:40.734
-Yeah, I hear you.
Yeah.

00:01:40.734 --> 00:01:42.200
You're gonna win.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:43.868
You have good taste.
-It's a lot of fun.

00:01:43.868 --> 00:01:46.434
-You have good taste.
Earlier this week, though,

00:01:46.434 --> 00:01:49.167
you were taping,
and something happened on set,

00:01:49.167 --> 00:01:52.534
and you had a mishap, and you
brought us exclusive footage

00:01:52.534 --> 00:01:53.934
and wanted everyone to see.

00:01:53.934 --> 00:01:56.667
Take a look at what happened
on set. This is Heidi Klum.

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:59.667
-Hi!

00:01:59.667 --> 00:02:02.400
Oh!
[ Audience gasps ]

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:06.067
[ Heidi laughs ]
[ Music stops ]

00:02:06.067 --> 00:02:07.701
-Are you okay?
-Yeah.

00:02:07.701 --> 00:02:09.234
-Hi.
-That was a fall.

00:02:09.234 --> 00:02:11.801
-Are you okay?
-Yes. I just --[ Laughs ]

00:02:11.801 --> 00:02:17.000
-You nearly pulled me down.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:20.467
-Yeah. Yeah.
-That's a fall.

00:02:20.467 --> 00:02:23.033
Oh, my God!
-I know. Did you hear Mel?

00:02:23.033 --> 00:02:24.868
-She was like,
"You almost pulled me down."

00:02:24.868 --> 00:02:26.567
She told me that four times.

00:02:26.567 --> 00:02:29.200
Simon just leaned over to me,
and he's like, "Make more --

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:31.200
Make more of it.
Make more of it."

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:32.434
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.434 --> 00:02:33.868
-Make it -- He's like,
"Are you okay?" "Yeah."

00:02:33.868 --> 00:02:35.200
"Make more of it.
Make a TV show."

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:37.400
-But it's so funny,
the schadenfreude that happens.

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:40.334
You know, the word, like, when
someone falls it's like --

00:02:40.334 --> 00:02:42.968
everyone was like, "Aah!"
It was just funny.

00:02:42.968 --> 00:02:45.767
-Everything went silent.
But then look at this, though.

00:02:45.767 --> 00:02:48.367
Your leg started bleeding.
-I mean, it literally

00:02:48.367 --> 00:02:50.334
looks like a cat scratch,
but it was deep.

00:02:50.334 --> 00:02:51.767
Someone had to come
and glue it shut.

00:02:51.767 --> 00:02:54.901
Have you ever had
something glued shut?

00:02:54.901 --> 00:02:57.934
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.934 --> 00:03:01.000
-Why are you looking up?
-No. [ Stammers ]

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:02.601
No.
-It's amazing.

00:03:02.601 --> 00:03:05.567
They put this superglue
in your wound, and it just ckk!

00:03:05.567 --> 00:03:07.501
-And that's instead of stitches.
-With, like, a little

00:03:07.501 --> 00:03:09.000
butterfly thing on it.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:11.567
-But Heidi Klum --
Heidi Klum's legs are like,

00:03:11.567 --> 00:03:13.901
you're like --
this is like Lloyds of London.

00:03:13.901 --> 00:03:15.334
I mean, this is insured by --

00:03:15.334 --> 00:03:17.200
Oh, you hurt your arm, too?
-Yeah.

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:19.734
I mean, honestly,
it looked funnier than it --

00:03:19.734 --> 00:03:22.467
-You can't do this
to Heidi Klum. This is --

00:03:22.467 --> 00:03:25.033
I know you're not American,
but you are an American --

00:03:25.033 --> 00:03:26.334
Yeah, you are.
-I am.

00:03:26.334 --> 00:03:27.934
What are you talking about?
I've been here longer

00:03:27.934 --> 00:03:29.133
than I have been in Germany.

00:03:29.133 --> 00:03:31.033
I have an American passport.
Ja.

00:03:31.033 --> 00:03:32.968
-Yeah, "Ja."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.968 --> 00:03:34.767
-Ja.
-Ja.

00:03:34.767 --> 00:03:37.100
-Yeah.
[ Applause ]

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:39.834
-I want to say happy birthday,
by the way.

00:03:39.834 --> 00:03:42.000
-50, yes.
That was fun. It still is.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:45.033
-There's you and Sofía Vergara.
-Ha!

00:03:45.033 --> 00:03:46.767
-Oh, I love her, too.
-I love her.

00:03:46.767 --> 00:03:48.834
No, this was --
My husband, you know, he's like,

00:03:48.834 --> 00:03:50.033
"Should we do a surprise party?"

00:03:50.033 --> 00:03:52.501
And I'm like, "Well,
there goes the surprise."

00:03:52.501 --> 00:03:53.934
-"You can't tell me.

00:03:53.934 --> 00:03:55.968
You can't tell me you're
throwing me a surprise party."

00:03:55.968 --> 00:03:57.267
-Yeah.
-That's the whole

00:03:57.267 --> 00:03:58.934
surprise of it, yeah.
-I would love one because,

00:03:58.934 --> 00:04:00.868
you know, otherwise, every year
is just another year,

00:04:00.868 --> 00:04:02.701
and you get older and older.
But I thought, "50?"

00:04:02.701 --> 00:04:05.000
I'm like, "Yes, go for it.
Make a big party."

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:07.868
And so we had, like,
a big, like, '20s-themed party.

00:04:07.868 --> 00:04:09.534
It was a lot of fun.
-Happy happy birthday.

00:04:09.534 --> 00:04:11.334
How is your husband, by the way?
-Hold are you now?

00:04:11.334 --> 00:04:12.801
-I'm 49.

00:04:12.801 --> 00:04:14.200
-Ah, so you're not there yet.
Almost.

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:15.701
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.701 --> 00:04:18.300
-How old do I --
How old do I look?

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:20.133
-49.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.133 --> 00:04:22.100
But, also, I have --
I can't see well.

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:24.734
I can only see far.
Like, this is, like -- yeah.

00:04:24.734 --> 00:04:26.434
It's all, like, very --
looks very good, yeah.

00:04:26.434 --> 00:04:28.000
-I'm gonna go all out for 50
and do something.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.000
-Like, my husband, because you
were talking about my husband,

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.434
my husband, you know,
he is doing --

00:04:32.434 --> 00:04:34.133
-He's the host of
"That's My Jam" in Germany.

00:04:34.133 --> 00:04:36.334
-"That's My Jam" in Germany.
And they just won, basically,

00:04:36.334 --> 00:04:38.634
the Emmy of Germany
for "That's My Jam."

00:04:38.634 --> 00:04:40.567
-Yeah. He's the best.
Give him my best.

00:04:40.567 --> 00:04:42.634
He's so funny.
Really talented.

00:04:42.634 --> 00:04:44.334
I love him.
Give him my best, please.

00:04:44.334 --> 00:04:46.067
And tell him congratulations.
-I will.

00:04:46.067 --> 00:04:48.767
-Halloween, it's a big deal.
You love Halloween.

00:04:48.767 --> 00:04:50.534
-For me, the biggest deal.
-Why, though?

00:04:50.534 --> 00:04:53.067
-I don't know. Because
I'm obsessed with Halloween,

00:04:53.067 --> 00:04:55.267
and I'm obsessed --
Yeah, Questlove is laughing

00:04:55.267 --> 00:04:57.133
because Questlove --
thank you so much --

00:04:57.133 --> 00:04:58.567
for years and years
and years and years,

00:04:58.567 --> 00:05:00.567
he always comes to my party,
and he makes sure

00:05:00.567 --> 00:05:02.567
that we all have the best time.
-He's the best.

00:05:02.567 --> 00:05:04.334
He D.J.'s your parties.
-The music, the best.

00:05:04.334 --> 00:05:07.634
And sometimes he literally
stays the end with me

00:05:07.634 --> 00:05:08.868
until they swoop us out.

00:05:08.868 --> 00:05:10.434
They're like,
"Can you please go home now?"

00:05:10.434 --> 00:05:11.834
-He's a great guy
to have at a party.

00:05:11.834 --> 00:05:14.667
But your Halloween costumes
are next level.

00:05:14.667 --> 00:05:15.734
Next level.
-Yeah, I love it.

00:05:15.734 --> 00:05:17.033
Because I love
the fantasy of it all.

00:05:17.033 --> 00:05:18.300
I love the fantasy.

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:21.167
I love becoming someone else
for people to guess.

00:05:21.167 --> 00:05:25.334
Last year, I was a cute
little rain worm and...

00:05:25.334 --> 00:05:26.834
-You want to see
the cute little rain worm?

00:05:26.834 --> 00:05:28.100
-Yeah, I was a cute
little rain worm.

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:31.100
-Look how frightening
is this thing. Oh, my God.

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:33.267
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]
-Yeah.

00:05:33.267 --> 00:05:35.167
Can we talk about
this back bend that I --

00:05:35.167 --> 00:05:36.367
Yeah, that was
a good back bend, yeah.

00:05:36.367 --> 00:05:37.701
-No, this was very hard.

00:05:37.701 --> 00:05:39.934
I was very claustrophobic
because basically they had

00:05:39.934 --> 00:05:43.300
to tie my arms down
in order to be in this position.

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:45.834
And then my face was, like,
glued to the outside of it,

00:05:45.834 --> 00:05:47.934
so I couldn't really move
my face any which way.

00:05:47.934 --> 00:05:49.234
I was just stuck.

00:05:49.234 --> 00:05:51.601
So three hours beforehand,
I wouldn't eat anymore.

00:05:51.601 --> 00:05:53.601
I wouldn't drink anything
because, I mean,

00:05:53.601 --> 00:05:55.734
I could have worn a diaper,
I guess, in there, but I didn't.

00:05:55.734 --> 00:05:57.567
-What are you talking about?
No, you're not wearing a...

00:05:57.567 --> 00:05:59.367
-I also could've just let it go.
No one would have known.

00:05:59.367 --> 00:06:00.901
-We have a video of you
and Quest, I think,

00:06:00.901 --> 00:06:02.434
from last year's party.

00:06:02.434 --> 00:06:05.601
-It's always the best.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:05.601 --> 00:06:10.000
-What is going on?

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:13.467
How are you acting --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:13.467 --> 00:06:17.234
First of all, how are you acting
like that's normal,

00:06:17.234 --> 00:06:19.200
like that's not happening
behind you?

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:20.667
There's a dancing worm
behind you.

00:06:20.667 --> 00:06:23.267
I -- You know, I just...
-Yeah, exactly.

00:06:23.267 --> 00:06:25.300
-He's always the best
because I never tell anyone.

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:27.133
So the first reaction
when you see me,

00:06:27.133 --> 00:06:30.234
you're always like me, "Neh."
-Yeah.

00:06:30.234 --> 00:06:32.834
You know what I think --
Of course you do so many things.

00:06:32.834 --> 00:06:34.901
You're so busy.
But I think you should host,

00:06:34.901 --> 00:06:37.334
like, a -- like, a
Halloween special for NBC.

00:06:37.334 --> 00:06:38.901
-I want to.
I would love to, yeah.

00:06:38.901 --> 00:06:40.000
-You should do it
like New Year's Eve or...

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:42.534
Yeah, where people
get to dress up.

00:06:42.534 --> 00:06:45.234
-Yes! And you got bands, and you
have a whole super party.

00:06:45.234 --> 00:06:46.367
-Yeah.
-You would do that?

00:06:46.367 --> 00:06:47.567
-Yeah, I would love it.
-See? That's --

00:06:47.567 --> 00:06:49.767
-Just I'm throwing out
ideas for you.

00:06:49.767 --> 00:06:51.334
What -- Can we see what
you're going to be?

00:06:51.334 --> 00:06:53.400
-I had this idea
before, obviously.

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:55.033
-No.
-You never said it on

00:06:55.033 --> 00:06:56.801
national television before.
-Well, you did.

00:06:56.801 --> 00:06:58.701
-Yeah. Here we go.
And so next year,

00:06:58.701 --> 00:07:01.868
the inaugural Heidi-Ween.
-Ooh, yes.

00:07:01.868 --> 00:07:03.067
-Yeah.
-Yes.

00:07:03.067 --> 00:07:04.801
[ Cheers and applause ]
See? They like the name.

00:07:04.801 --> 00:07:07.200
-Yes.
-I came up with the --

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:08.634
I came up with the name, too.

00:07:08.634 --> 00:07:11.133
What -- Can you hint at what
you're going to be this year?

00:07:11.133 --> 00:07:14.100
-No, because, you know, I always
like it for it to be a surprise.

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:15.868
Otherwise, people are like,
"Oh, she's gonna be this,"

00:07:15.868 --> 00:07:17.267
and then I show up,
and they're like,

00:07:17.267 --> 00:07:19.367
"Eh, it wasn't as good as I
thought she was gonna do."

00:07:19.367 --> 00:07:21.834
So I always think it's never
good to talk about it.

00:07:21.834 --> 00:07:23.968
-Okay.
-But it's gonna be gigantic.

00:07:23.968 --> 00:07:26.601
And I have to close a few
streets down here in Manhattan,

00:07:26.601 --> 00:07:28.801
which is very hard to do,
by the way.

00:07:28.801 --> 00:07:30.934
[ Laughter ]

00:07:30.934 --> 00:07:33.434
-Yes.
-Wait. So it's a giant costume?

00:07:33.434 --> 00:07:35.334
You have to close streets down?
-Yeah.

00:07:35.334 --> 00:07:37.501
-Are you a Transformer?
Like, an 18-wheeler?

00:07:37.501 --> 00:07:39.501
-It's really.
-Are you like a robot?

00:07:39.501 --> 00:07:41.701
A giant truck robot
that transforms.

00:07:41.701 --> 00:07:43.501
-It's really big.
-I guessed it.

00:07:43.501 --> 00:07:44.701
-No, you didn't.
-Yeah, I did.

00:07:44.701 --> 00:07:47.467
-I swear.
-No, I know it, I know it.

00:07:47.467 --> 00:07:49.601
Now you have to change
your costume.

00:07:49.601 --> 00:07:52.601
[ Laughter ]

00:07:52.601 --> 00:07:54.234
I love it.
-I swear, I'm not.

00:07:54.234 --> 00:07:55.767
-I love it when you
come on the show,

00:07:55.767 --> 00:07:57.868
and I cannot wait to see what
you're gonna do this year.

00:07:57.868 --> 00:07:59.634
You're always the best.
Heidi Klum, everybody.

00:07:59.634 --> 00:08:01.868
"America's Got Talent:
Fantasy League"

00:08:01.868 --> 00:08:04.234
premieres in January on NBC.

00:08:04.234 --> 00:08:05.734
More "Tonight Show"
after the break.

00:08:05.734 --> 00:08:07.467
Stick around everybody.

